1
00:00:01,921 --> 00:00:03,298
Hoo, hoo!

2
00:00:03,410 --> 00:00:04,337
Hi!

3
00:00:04,387 --> 00:00:06,414
It's me, Popcorn!

4
00:00:06,536 --> 00:00:11,767
Welcome to Popcorn Tales, the
cozy nest of bedtime stories.

5
00:00:12,079 --> 00:00:15,505
Hug your teddy, because
tonight's story is:

6
00:00:15,555 --> 00:00:17,765
The Emperor's New Clothes!

7
00:00:22,374 --> 00:00:28,310
Once upon a time, in a very cheerful
kingdom, there lived an emperor who loved

8
00:00:28,360 --> 00:00:32,371
new clothes more than anything
else in the whole world.

9
00:00:33,047 --> 00:00:37,747
He had a different coat for every
hour of the day, and he spent entire

10
00:00:37,797 --> 00:00:42,844
mornings in front of the mirror, trying
on hats, boots and capes of every

11
00:00:42,894 --> 00:00:44,094
color.

12
00:00:44,375 --> 00:00:48,208
This blue coat looks lovely, but I
think the green one goes better with my

13
00:00:48,258 --> 00:00:49,131
crown,

14
00:00:49,181 --> 00:00:52,998
the emperor said, turning
around in front of the mirror.

15
00:00:53,615 --> 00:00:57,468
Whenever someone came to talk to
the emperor about roads or schools,

16
00:00:57,518 --> 00:01:02,724
the guards always gave the same answer,
that he was busy in his dressing room.

17
00:01:03,316 --> 00:01:04,693
Hoo, hoo!

18
00:01:04,790 --> 00:01:09,786
This emperor changes his clothes
more often than I change my feathers.

19
00:01:10,058 --> 00:01:12,435
Let's see where all this is going,

20
00:01:12,485 --> 00:01:15,108
Popcorn said, from the window.

21
00:01:17,386 --> 00:01:22,586
One day, two strangers arrived at the
palace, saying they were the finest

22
00:01:22,636 --> 00:01:24,370
weavers in the world.

23
00:01:24,990 --> 00:01:29,760
One was tall and thin and his name was
Bartolo, and the other was short and

24
00:01:29,810 --> 00:01:32,238
round and his name was Fausto.

25
00:01:32,852 --> 00:01:37,189
Your Majesty, we can weave a cloth so
fine and so beautiful that no king has

26
00:01:37,239 --> 00:01:38,786
ever worn anything like it,

27
00:01:38,836 --> 00:01:42,763
Bartolo said, with a very exaggerated bow.

28
00:01:43,349 --> 00:01:46,141
And this cloth has a wonderful
secret, Your Majesty:

29
00:01:46,191 --> 00:01:49,679
it becomes invisible to anyone who is
very foolish, or who is not good at

30
00:01:49,729 --> 00:01:50,752
their own job,

31
00:01:50,802 --> 00:01:53,350
Fausto added, with a wink.

32
00:01:53,989 --> 00:01:57,638
The emperor loved the idea,
and he thought out loud:

33
00:01:57,688 --> 00:02:01,933
With clothes like that, I will find
out who is clever and who is not in my

34
00:02:01,983 --> 00:02:03,183
kingdom!

35
00:02:03,692 --> 00:02:06,976
He ordered a big sack full of
gold coins for the two of them,

36
00:02:07,026 --> 00:02:09,829
so they could start
working that very same day.

37
00:02:10,929 --> 00:02:15,129
The two weavers set up two large
looms in a room of the palace,

38
00:02:15,179 --> 00:02:19,268
and began moving their hands in the
air, as if they were weaving very

39
00:02:19,318 --> 00:02:20,518
carefully.

40
00:02:21,092 --> 00:02:26,770
But the looms were completely empty,
without a single thread of wool or silk.

41
00:02:27,386 --> 00:02:31,829
We need more fine silk and more golden
thread, so the cloth will be perfect,

42
00:02:31,879 --> 00:02:35,224
they asked the palace
steward every single day.

43
00:02:35,875 --> 00:02:39,992
The steward brought them everything,
and the two of them hid the silk and the

44
00:02:40,042 --> 00:02:45,261
gold in a chest, and kept on weaving
the empty air until late at night.

45
00:02:45,407 --> 00:02:49,010
Soon the news of the magic cloth
spread through the whole city,

46
00:02:49,060 --> 00:02:54,252
and everybody was curious to find out
who was foolish and who was clever.

47
00:02:54,892 --> 00:02:59,050
In the bakeries, at the markets and
in the squares, people talked about

48
00:02:59,100 --> 00:03:03,236
nothing but the enchanted cloth
being woven at the palace.

49
00:03:03,820 --> 00:03:05,197
Hoo, hoo!

50
00:03:05,321 --> 00:03:10,597
I'm looking very closely, and I can't
see a single thread on those looms,

51
00:03:10,647 --> 00:03:13,922
Popcorn whispered, with a suspicious look.

52
00:03:15,013 --> 00:03:19,657
After a few days, the emperor became
curious to know how the cloth was coming

53
00:03:19,707 --> 00:03:20,907
along.

54
00:03:21,321 --> 00:03:24,928
But the emperor was also a little
bit worried, and he thought:

55
00:03:24,978 --> 00:03:27,027
What if I can't see the cloth?

56
00:03:27,114 --> 00:03:30,947
I'd better send my old minister first,
because he is the most honest man in

57
00:03:30,997 --> 00:03:32,197
the kingdom.

58
00:03:32,646 --> 00:03:36,943
The old minister went to the workshop,
straightened his round glasses,

59
00:03:36,993 --> 00:03:40,046
and looked at the looms
with all his attention.

60
00:03:40,684 --> 00:03:45,159
The minister's eyes grew wide,
and he thought, in a panic:

61
00:03:45,209 --> 00:03:48,720
Oh my goodness, I can't
see anything at all!

62
00:03:48,866 --> 00:03:50,345
Am I foolish?

63
00:03:50,477 --> 00:03:52,809
Nobody must ever find out!

64
00:03:53,401 --> 00:03:55,593
Isn't it lovely, dear minister?

65
00:03:55,709 --> 00:03:58,846
Look at these cheerful colors,
and this delicate pattern,

66
00:03:58,896 --> 00:04:01,824
Fausto said, pointing at nothing.

67
00:04:02,415 --> 00:04:08,032
Yes, indeed, it is very beautiful, and
I will tell the emperor all about it,

68
00:04:08,082 --> 00:04:12,121
the minister answered, with
a slightly shaky voice.

69
00:04:12,748 --> 00:04:17,893
The next day, the emperor also sent his
treasurer, a very serious gentleman in

70
00:04:17,943 --> 00:04:21,773
a tall hat, and exactly
the same thing happened.

71
00:04:22,403 --> 00:04:26,284
The treasurer saw nothing,
was afraid of looking foolish,

72
00:04:26,334 --> 00:04:30,603
and came back saying it was the most
beautiful cloth he had ever seen in his

73
00:04:30,653 --> 00:04:31,853
whole life.

74
00:04:32,903 --> 00:04:38,284
At last, the emperor himself went to see
the cloth, with all his ministers and

75
00:04:38,334 --> 00:04:40,748
chamberlains walking behind him.

76
00:04:41,431 --> 00:04:47,164
The emperor looked, and looked again,
and saw absolutely nothing on the looms.

77
00:04:47,778 --> 00:04:49,850
The emperor thought, very worried:

78
00:04:49,900 --> 00:04:51,231
How terrible!

79
00:04:51,320 --> 00:04:53,396
Am I not good enough to be emperor?

80
00:04:53,486 --> 00:04:55,549
Nobody can ever notice!

81
00:04:56,086 --> 00:05:00,171
How marvelous, what a beautiful
cloth, I simply love it!

82
00:05:00,221 --> 00:05:04,635
the emperor said, very
loudly, clapping his hands.

83
00:05:05,272 --> 00:05:09,833
And all the ministers and chamberlains,
who could not see anything either,

84
00:05:09,883 --> 00:05:14,380
began to praise the cloth,
each one louder than the last.

85
00:05:14,950 --> 00:05:19,601
Your Majesty, you should wear these new
clothes in the grand parade tomorrow,

86
00:05:19,651 --> 00:05:21,889
and the whole city will admire you,

87
00:05:21,939 --> 00:05:23,991
the old minister suggested.

88
00:05:25,076 --> 00:05:29,068
On the morning of the parade, the
weavers snipped the air with enormous

89
00:05:29,118 --> 00:05:33,476
scissors and sewed with needles
that had no thread at all.

90
00:05:35,212 --> 00:05:37,307
There you are, Your Majesty!

91
00:05:37,489 --> 00:05:41,129
Your new clothes are ready, and they
are so light that it feels as if you are

92
00:05:41,179 --> 00:05:42,543
wearing nothing at all,

93
00:05:42,593 --> 00:05:45,590
Bartolo said, with a clever grin.

94
00:05:46,239 --> 00:05:50,412
The emperor took off his red robe,
and stood there in his long striped

95
00:05:50,462 --> 00:05:53,473
underwear and a plain white undershirt.

96
00:05:54,088 --> 00:05:58,732
The weavers pretended to dress him in
a coat, a pair of trousers and a very

97
00:05:58,782 --> 00:06:03,002
long cape, and the emperor turned
around in front of the mirror,

98
00:06:03,074 --> 00:06:05,030
feeling very proud.

99
00:06:05,658 --> 00:06:10,364
Two chamberlains bent down and
pretended to hold the train of the cape,

100
00:06:10,436 --> 00:06:13,475
with their hands closed
around the empty air.

101
00:06:14,062 --> 00:06:15,439
Hoo, hoo!

102
00:06:15,551 --> 00:06:20,822
I have to cover my beak with my wing,
or else I will laugh much too loudly,

103
00:06:20,872 --> 00:06:23,911
Popcorn said, shaking with giggles.

104
00:06:28,168 --> 00:06:32,452
The band began to play, and the emperor
marched through the city under a red

105
00:06:32,502 --> 00:06:35,402
canopy, with his chin held high.

106
00:06:36,072 --> 00:06:39,675
The people on the sidewalks had
heard all about the magic cloth,

107
00:06:39,725 --> 00:06:42,208
and nobody wanted to look foolish.

108
00:06:42,855 --> 00:06:44,838
What lovely clothes!

109
00:06:45,060 --> 00:06:46,779
What a long cape!

110
00:06:46,990 --> 00:06:48,908
What wonderful colors!

111
00:06:48,958 --> 00:06:52,566
everyone shouted, all at the same time.

112
00:06:53,226 --> 00:06:56,918
In the middle of the crowd,
there was a girl named Lia,

113
00:06:57,004 --> 00:07:01,134
sitting on her father's shoulders,
and she looked at the emperor very

114
00:07:01,184 --> 00:07:02,384
carefully.

115
00:07:02,938 --> 00:07:07,213
Daddy, look, the emperor is walking
around in his striped underwear and his

116
00:07:07,263 --> 00:07:08,255
undershirt!

117
00:07:08,305 --> 00:07:12,733
Lia said, very loudly,
and with complete honesty.

118
00:07:13,446 --> 00:07:16,993
The street went quiet for a moment,
and then somebody repeated it,

119
00:07:17,043 --> 00:07:20,388
and somebody else, until
the whole city was saying:

120
00:07:20,443 --> 00:07:23,232
It's true, he's in his underwear!

121
00:07:24,346 --> 00:07:28,907
The emperor felt the cool breeze on
his legs, and he turned as red as a

122
00:07:28,957 --> 00:07:30,157
tomato.

123
00:07:36,941 --> 00:07:42,197
But instead of getting angry, he started
to laugh, and he laughed so hard that

124
00:07:42,247 --> 00:07:44,633
his crown nearly fell off his head.

125
00:07:45,193 --> 00:07:48,332
The girl is right, and
I have been very vain!

126
00:07:48,563 --> 00:07:52,101
Thank you, Lia, for being
brave enough to tell the truth,

127
00:07:52,151 --> 00:07:57,023
the emperor said, wrapped in a
blanket that Lia's mother lent him.

128
00:07:57,683 --> 00:08:00,999
The two weavers tried to
sneak away down a back street,

129
00:08:01,058 --> 00:08:05,319
but Popcorn flew right in front
of them, flapping her wings.

130
00:08:05,861 --> 00:08:09,514
We are sorry, Your Majesty, we fooled
everyone, and we will give back all the

131
00:08:09,564 --> 00:08:10,987
gold and all the silk,

132
00:08:11,037 --> 00:08:14,337
Fausto said, looking down at his shoes.

133
00:08:14,962 --> 00:08:18,932
The emperor forgave them both,
and gave them a real job:

134
00:08:19,073 --> 00:08:23,098
weaving warm blankets for the
families of the city in the winter.

135
00:08:23,728 --> 00:08:28,123
And from that day on, the emperor
spent less time in front of the mirror,

136
00:08:28,173 --> 00:08:31,239
and much more time taking
care of his people.

137
00:08:31,809 --> 00:08:33,186
Hoo, hoo!

138
00:08:33,313 --> 00:08:38,028
Telling the truth kindly is what
brave people do, just like Lia,

139
00:08:38,078 --> 00:08:41,450
Popcorn said, blinking her big eyes.

140
00:08:48,754 --> 00:08:49,954
The End.

141
00:08:51,669 --> 00:08:52,381
Hoo...

142
00:08:52,431 --> 00:08:53,456
Psst!

143
00:08:53,506 --> 00:08:55,078
Are you still awake?

144
00:08:55,230 --> 00:08:57,284
Did you like tonight's story?

145
00:08:57,411 --> 00:09:01,788
Lia showed us that telling the
truth kindly is a kind of courage,

146
00:09:01,838 --> 00:09:05,728
and that we never need to pretend
just to please other people.

147
00:09:06,005 --> 00:09:10,311
Good night, sleep tight, and
have the sweetest dreams.

148
00:09:10,607 --> 00:09:15,505
Grown-ups: if you enjoyed it,
please subscribe to Popcorn Tales,

149
00:09:15,555 --> 00:09:17,960
for more stories at bedtime.

150
00:09:18,264 --> 00:09:19,464
Hoo...

